# Source repair of J.2.7(5–6)

This boundary proves the odd-complement reduction, the hyperplane factorization
and order formula, and the final five-core/nonconjugacy assembly, retaining
the original Sylow five-subgroup and every ambient map. The assembly is
conditional on the local quaternion calculation and odd-subgroup bound,
the z-class inverter and its action, and the M₁₀ order-45 exclusion and
residual Sylow order. Those constructions remain required for J.2.7(5–6).
The legacy FiveCore records are preserved but are not used as source
witnesses here. In particular, no unconditional containment of the odd
core in the cubic centralizer is asserted.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, printed pp.435–436 (PDF pp.446–447).
-/
